Machine Strike in Horizon Forbidden West has always been you against the computer. Strikers lets you play it against a friend instead, online, with each of you in your own copy of the game. You both start a normal Machine Strike challenge, and the computer opponent on your screen plays your friend's moves.

[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Play Machine Strike online against a friend.
[*]Build your own boards, any size up to 8 by 8, with whatever terrain you like on each square.
[*]Build your own armies from the game's machines.
[*]Pick how many victory points it takes to win and how much an army can cost.
[*]Share boards and armies with a short text code.
[*]No port forwarding or router setup.
[*]Neither of you sees the other's IP address.
[/list]

[b]Back up your saves first.[/b] Strikers changes the game while a match is running, and the game keeps saving as you play, so it's worth having a copy. Your saves are in Documents\Horizon Forbidden West Complete Edition. Copy that folder somewhere safe.

[size=4][b]What you'll both need[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Windows 10 or 11.
[*]Horizon Forbidden West Complete Edition on Steam, one copy each.
[*]The same version of the game. Update it in Steam on both PCs. If the versions don't match, Strikers will tell you and won't start the match.
[*]The same version of Strikers.
[*]A save that's reached Salma's Machine Strike table in Chainscrape.
[*]Regular Challenge unlocked at Salma's table. Every match runs through that challenge, whatever board and armies you pick. To unlock it, beat Beginner's Practice: Easy, Medium and Hard. Or close the challenge list, press Unlock challenges in Strikers' Settings, and open the list again. That unlock lasts until you restart the game.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installing[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Unzip Strikers.zip anywhere and run Strikers.exe. Nothing gets installed and no game files are touched. To remove it, delete the folder.
[*]Windows will warn you about an unknown publisher, because the download isn't signed. Press More info, then Run anyway.
[*]Strikers won't run with Windows Smart App Control turned on. If Windows blocks live-probe.exe, turn Smart App Control off.
[*]Your antivirus might flag live-probe.exe. That's the part of Strikers that reads and writes the game's memory during a match.
[*]If you want to check that your download is genuine, the Strikers GitHub page (linked at the bottom) shows you how.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Playing a match[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*][b]Both of you, in the game:[/b] go to Salma in Chainscrape, choose Machine Strike, then Challenges. Stay on the challenge list and don't go into a challenge yet.
[*][b]Both:[/b] open Strikers.exe. One of you hosts, which means setting up the match, and the other joins.
[*][b]Host:[/b] under Host, pick the board, the victory points to win, the max army cost and who goes first, then press Create invite. The invite is a line of text. Press Copy and send it to your friend privately, in a direct message for example. It lasts ten minutes, and New invite gives you a fresh one. Anyone who has the invite can join, so keep it between the two of you.
[*][b]Joiner:[/b] copy the invite you were sent, then under Join press Paste, then Join. The board and rules come with it.
[*][b]Both:[/b] pick an army and press Use this army. Once the host has picked, the joiner can choose Opponent's army so you both play the same one. Make your army in the Armies panel before you create or join an invite, because you can't get back to that panel afterwards.
[*][b]Both:[/b] check the safety code. Press the eye button to see your four characters and read them out to your friend, over voice or chat. Type the four they read to you into the Theirs squares. When they match, Continue lights up, so press it. If it doesn't light up, check the code with each other. If no code shows up at all, press Stop and start again.
[*][b]Both:[/b] with the game still on the challenge list, press Set up the match. It takes about half a minute.
[*][b]Both:[/b] wait for the green You are both ready message before you go into the challenge. If you go in early, your boards won't match. Once it appears you've got ten minutes, and a countdown shows how long is left.
[*][b]Both:[/b] go straight from the challenge list into Regular Challenge and place your machines, taking turns.
[*][b]Play:[/b] take your turns in the game like normal. Strikers sends each one to your friend, and their turns play out on your board as the computer opponent's. You don't need to touch Strikers during the match.
[/list]
Keep Strikers open on both PCs until the match is over. If either of you closes it, the match ends. When it's done, press Continue in the game, then Stop in Strikers. To play again, start from Create invite.

[size=4][b]If something goes wrong[/b][/size]
If a match stops with an error, Strikers puts together a report, which takes under a minute, and then shows a [b]Send report[/b] button. That opens the folder with the report in it and a new bug report on the Strikers GitHub page. Drag the report in and say what was happening in the game just before it stopped. One report is usually enough, and the screen will tell you if you should both send one.

[size=4][b]What Strikers does on your PC[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]It doesn't install anything or change any game files.
[*]During a match it reads and writes the game's memory, and changes a few parts of the game's code in memory so the computer opponent plays your friend's moves. Those changes are undone when the match ends, and closing the game clears everything else.
[*]If a match stops, each PC sends the other a record of the board positions and the end of its Strikers log, so both of your reports have both sides. Player names, army names, codes and folder paths are blanked out first.
[*]A report holds your Strikers log, the end of your friend's, and both records of the match, with the same things blanked out. It stays on your PC until you send it.
[*]Settings, armies, boards, logs, match records and reports all live in the Strikers folder, and they stay there until you delete it.
[*]Your IP address is never shown to the other player. Both PCs connect through bore.pub, a free public service that passes the connection along, and everything sent through it is encrypted so only the two of you can read it.
[*]It offers to download a background picture and a window icon from files.catbox.moe, a file host. Both are images from the game. If you say no, Strikers runs fine without them.
[*]Each time it starts, it checks Nexus Mods and GitHub for a newer version. It doesn't send anything about you or your games.
[/list]
This mod changes a single-player game on your own PC, and the game's publisher doesn't support it.


Source code and issues: [url=https://github.com/everydayaussie/Strikers]https://github.com/everydayaussie/Strikers[/url]
